********Dependancy --> means --> Field **************** 

1. Instantiation:-> 
** There are Three ways to Bean Instantiation.
 1. simple<bean> :- e.g:- <bean> id="emp" class="com.main.app.Employee" <beam/>
--> Spring will be use the default constructor no logic no value
 
 2. Simple bean with some dependecy :-
 <bean> : <property> or <construct-arg>   </bean>

 3. Simple bean with some logic (Java Code)  
    ----> static Factory method
   --> Add custom logic of object creation (UUID)
   ** if you want logic like UUID Generation or some default during cretion then 
     <bean id="emp" class="com.mainapp.ObjectFactory"  factory-method="getObject" />
   ** this is the static factory method approach
--> but Spring cannot inject dependencies like Account inside that method directly b/c spring doesn't manage static methods internals.

***** Seperation Concern
 4. Complex bean with some logic (java code) 
     ......> use instance factory method 
--> Add Logic + dependecy injection uuid(Universe Unique Identifier) + Account from Spring).
